1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:07,494
The brush clears a vessel with a wide, flared rim. It is a chalice, from the age of the Shungas.

2
00:00:07,494 --> 00:00:13,553
After Ashoka, the empire did not last long. Who ruled after the Mauryas?

3
00:00:31,850 --> 00:00:37,234
How do we know? Archaeologists dug up Shunga towns and the railings of Bharhut.

4
00:00:37,234 --> 00:00:46,539
The Puranas and a play, the Malavikagnimitra, name the kings. An inscription at Ayodhya mentions Pushyamitra's sacrifices.

5
00:01:03,350 --> 00:01:10,219
Ashoka died about 232 BCE. His successors were weaker, and the empire shrank.

6
00:01:10,219 --> 00:01:19,275
The last Mauryan king, Brihadratha, was killed about 185 BCE by his own commander, Pushyamitra Shunga, who took the throne.

7
00:01:19,275 --> 00:01:22,699
The Shungas ruled from Pataliputra and Vidisha.

8
00:01:22,699 --> 00:01:31,794
Pushyamitra performed the Ashvamedha sacrifice, according to an Ayodhya inscription. Patanjali, the grammarian, lived in his time.

9
00:01:31,794 --> 00:01:36,104
The Bharhut stupa was enlarged in Shunga times, with a carved railing.

10
00:01:36,104 --> 00:01:45,729
The Shungas gave way, about 73 BCE, to the Kanvas, a short-lived family of Brahmin kings. They ruled for about forty-five years.

11
00:01:45,729 --> 00:01:51,840
After them, the Magadhan kings were overtaken by new powers, in the Deccan and the north-west.

12
00:02:08,650 --> 00:02:16,744
Scholars disagree. Why did the Maurya empire fall? One view blames reaction among Brahmins to Ashoka's policies.

13
00:02:16,744 --> 00:02:24,131
Another view points to financial strain from the army and officers, weak successors, and distant provinces drifting away.

14
00:02:24,131 --> 00:02:28,092
Most historians now look to the second set of reasons.

15
00:02:44,917 --> 00:02:56,481
Carve this tip into memory. Brihadratha killed, 185 BCE:. Shungas, then Kanvas. One killing, one date, two short dynasties.

16
00:02:56,481 --> 00:02:59,527
That is the aftermath of the Mauryas.

17
00:03:16,350 --> 00:03:32,878
Dig Quiz. Pause and name it. Number one. Who killed the last Mauryan king? The answer: Pushyamitra Shunga. Number two.

18
00:03:32,878 --> 00:03:44,631
Which stupa was enlarged with a carved railing in Shunga times? The answer: Bharhut. Number three.

19
00:03:44,631 --> 00:03:56,627
Which grammarian lived in Pushyamitra’s time? The answer: Patanjali. Now one line for Mains.

20
00:03:56,627 --> 00:04:00,633
Discuss the causes of the decline of the Mauryan empire.

21
00:04:21,450 --> 00:04:28,601
The chalice goes into its case. It comes from the small courts of the Shungas. Three facts to take away.

22
00:04:28,601 --> 00:04:36,628
A flared vessel of Shunga times. Shungas ruled from about 185 BCE. Followed by the Kanvas.

23
00:04:36,628 --> 00:04:41,058
Next gallery: Greeks, Shakas and Parthians.

